# Care Reality Language (Not Care Notes)

**SoT:** [`docs/02-product/solenos-care-reality-language.md`](../../docs/02-product/solenos-care-reality-language.md)

## Never (caregiver-facing)

Care notes · stored/saved notes · note history · supporting notes · more complete records · evidence maturity · lower attention items · “added to your care notes” · “your notes show” · “previous entries” · “I saved a note”

## Use

What we understand · what changed · what connects · still unclear · before/after · needs attention now · Care Story

## Pipeline

Message → Care Reality → Meaning → Connection → Care Story Update → Understanding  
Never: Message → Note → Summary

## Plain American English

- Use familiar American English, short sentences, and active voice.
- Use American spelling: behavior, organize, organization, prioritize, color, center, recognize.
- Never expose engineering, database, AI-processing, or unexplained clinical terminology.
- Avoid: epistemic status, provenance, reconciliation, assertion, extraction pipeline, OCR, API, JSON, schema, database, model inference.
- Preserve who reported something, when it happened, and what remains uncertain.
- Simplify wording without increasing certainty.

**Feel:** SolenOS understands what is happening — never stores notes.  
Examples in the SoT are illustrations only — never product if-branches.
